hree new properties. Without that the existing test fails. It has the side benefit of pinning the new payload at the render-to-request level.\n\nTests cover both levels the ticket asks for: a unit test that the generated payload contains `dead: false` plus the three explicit nulls, and a request-level test asserting on the body actually handed to `savePatient`. Both fail without the fix. The coded and non-coded cause-of-death paths are also covered so the `isDead: true` behaviour stays pinned.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n## Related Issue\n\nhttps://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5919\n\n## Other\n\nVerified with `yarn verify` (27/27 tasks), the full registration suite (38 files, 283 passing), `tsc`, `eslint` and a production build. FHIR still represents the patient as not deceased, since `mapPatientToFhirPatient` derives `deceasedBoolean` from `dead`.\n","nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012eTVhFzrnnW8828AXD77jW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
